From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter B Hough <git@hough.ink>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 22:12:40 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 158/159] refactor(refinery): retire the merge approval gate
 and keep the origin-scoped PR repo (gcp-648nn)

Hunter ruled to retire the fork's gc-native merge approval gate (option A,
keep the origin repo scoping). It is fork-only, has been disarmed in every
rig since 2026-09-08, partly duplicates upstream #245's PR-review lane, and
re-conflicts with the mr lane on every baseline upgrade.

With no gate, the refinery's mr lane is upstream #245's: open or reuse the
PR, `pr-merge-reconcile record`, and the bead stays blocked until reconcile
closes it on a verified GitHub merge. The origin-repo scoping of the PR
lookup (resolve_origin_repo and --repo "$ORIGIN_REPO") stays, since upstream's
`gh repo view` resolves to the fork's parent repo.

Retired, by subject and bead id (this is one forward commit, not a history
rewrite):
- gcp-dc8: the approval signal (record-merge-approval.sh), the fail-closed
  merge-approval-gate.sh, the patrol gate, and the flatten/guard of the
  refusal metadata write
- gcp-amo: resolving the gate from the formula's own pack tree
- gcp-3ty: scoping the gate's PR lookup to origin
- gcp-a22: resolving the review nudge across both agent scopes
- "an approved mr landing closes with verified-PR evidence (gcp-fooz4)":
  the 4b lane and its direct_close mr arm

Removed: the three gate files, merge-push.sh's approval resolution, park and
4b code (direct_close is back to its single-lane form, exit 4 is gone),
merge-batch.sh's gate guards (including the unreadable-config fail-closed,
whose only rationale was the approval switch), the formula's vars and prose
and exit-4 row, the README section, and their tests and pins. A city that
still sets require_merge_approval or review_agent in [rigs.formula_vars]
carries dead config, not an error.

Validation: test_refinery_merge_lanes (22 cases), test_refinery_merge_batch
(22 cases), test_refinery_merge_push and test_polecat_artifact_dir pass; the
AC1 grep prints only the two historical gcp-amo comments in the deacon and
witness patrols.

Fold at the next baseline upgrade: drop those patches and fix up this commit's remaining hunks into their introducing patches; the replayed tree must equal the pre-fold tree (gcp-k6301).

